{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-11-05 22:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. You’re here today for a planned surgery to create a new dialysis access in your left arm, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-11-05 22:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been on dialysis through the catheter in my neck, but they said it’s better to have a graft in my arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-11-05 22:23:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re going to place a loop graft in your left arm so you can have more reliable and safer long-term dialysis access."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-11-05 22:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I heard they might use a synthetic tube. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-11-05 22:26:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we used a PTFE graft because your vessels have some calcification. It’s a strong, safe material that works well for patients like you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-11-05 22:27:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m a little worried about my hand going numb or cold after this. I’ve had circulation issues before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-11-05 22:28:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a valid concern. We checked during surgery, and there’s a good pulse in your wrist. Your hand is a bit cooler than the other side, but that’s expected and close to your baseline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-11-05 22:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the numbness in my fingertips? That’s been there a while, but I don’t want it to get worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-11-05 22:31:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You mentioned mild numbness, which we believe is related to your diabetic neuropathy. We didn’t see any new nerve issues from the surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-11-05 23:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. How’s your left arm feeling? Any pain, coldness, or blue fingers?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-11-05 23:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No pain, no blue fingers. It’s still a little cool, and the tips of my fingers are numb like usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-11-05 23:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’re watching closely for any signs of poor blood flow. The graft has a strong thrill and bruit, which means it’s working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-11-06 06:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You just finished your dialysis session through the neck catheter. Everything went smoothly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-11-06 06:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. So now what? Is the new graft ready to use?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-11-06 06:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. It needs about 2–3 weeks to mature before we can use it for dialysis. You’ll keep using your neck catheter until then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-11-06 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you today. Your graft is patent, and your hand exam remains stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-11-06 12:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should I watch for at home? I don’t want to miss anything serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-11-06 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call the access clinic immediately if you have fevers, pain, coldness, or blue fingers in the left hand. Also check daily for the thrill—the buzzing feeling over the graft."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-11-06 12:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I don’t feel the buzz?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-11-06 12:05:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could mean the graft is blocked. Call right away—don’t wait for your next dialysis. Also, no blood pressures or needle sticks in that arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-11-06 12:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No heavy lifting either, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-11-06 12:08:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Keep it under 10 pounds, and avoid tight clothes or jewelry on that side. Elevate your arm to reduce swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-11-06 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge orders are ready. You’ll continue all your regular medications, including insulin and apixaban."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-11-06 15:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the pain medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-11-06 15:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have tramadol for mild pain and now also hydrocodone for breakthrough pain—take only as needed. And we added docusate for constipation prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-11-06 15:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel ready to go home now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-11-06 15:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Keep your follow-up with the access team, and continue dialysis as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-11-06 17:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. You’re cleared to go home with services. Take care, and call if anything changes with your arm."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-11-05 22:21:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-11-06 17:13:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis was admitted for elective placement of a left arm AV loop graft. Due to vessel calcification, a PTFE graft was placed successfully. She was monitored overnight for hand ischemia and neuropathy symptoms, which remained stable. She received hemodialysis via her existing tunneled catheter and was discharged home the following day with instructions to monitor graft function, avoid venipuncture or blood pressure measurements in the left arm, and follow up with the access clinic. No complications were observed during the admission.",
